            <ArticleTitle>[Physical training of patients with ischemic heart disease in a sanatorium-preventorium].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>36-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with coronary heart disease were shown to benefit from short-term training sessions on the stationary bicycle (15-18 sessions within 24 days). In a group of 96 patients who exercised, the threshold power increased by 20%, the blood cholesterol concentration fell slightly (by 6.4%) and the systolic and diastolic pressure decreased in those patients who showed an initial elevated arterial pressure at rest (160/95 mm Hg). The follow-up examination of 24 patients at one year revealed that the majority of the patients had stopped training mostly due to the lack of spare time.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
